  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that capsaicin may interact with the DNMT3A2/3L complex through a series of intermediate targets, primarily the sodium/bile acid cotransporter. Capsaicin is known to target this transporter, which is involved in bile acid transport and has been implicated in various physiological and pathological processes. The sodium/bile acid cotransporter is also a target of other compounds, such as 1-(Acetyloxy)-1,2-dihydroobacunoic acid eta-lactone and 14,15-Dimethoxy-20-methyl-5,7-dioxa-20-azapentacyclo[10.5.3.01,13.02,10.04,8]icosa-2,4(8),9,14-tetraene-16,19-dione, which themselves are linked to the DNMT3A2/3L complex. This indicates a potential pathway where capsaicin may influence the DNMT3A2/3L complex through the sodium/bile acid cotransporter, possibly by modulating the activity of these compounds or by affecting the cellular environment in which they operate. The scores from the different paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, but further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the direct interaction between capsaicin and the DNMT3A2/3L complex.",
